					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-754769#post-1940701</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-754769/where-the-garden-began#post-1940701</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Mon, 20 Jan 2014 11:41:19 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>Gavon</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>1347106</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>(Crudely copying this here since few use the Facebook page)<br /> Holy crap, this was a positively gorgeous metaphor, and highlights some of the problems the wiki still struggles with, such as lack of positive reinforcement, acknowledgement that the mere fact that they're creating - even if the flowers they raise now are sad and misshaped - is the first step to creating ones with beauty yet unimagined.<br /> So little if any encouragement to keep writing, keep creating, learn, so that you may one day begin to create better.</p> <p>I will always have some measure of awe for authors that can create something entirely from scratch, even if their writing is stilted and awkward, it's still far more than many others (including me) manage to create, and I can see little save potential.</p> <p>After all, they have the drive. Merely that they have the drive to create means that with training their potential for beauty is limitless.</p> <p>So why do we shun the ugly duckling, when it is trying to take the first steps to becoming a beautiful swan?</p> <p>I'd hug you for this if I could, Bryvx. Few things inspire rants like these from me.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
